values ('c6d7e8f9-1a2b-4c66-9d56-6e7f8a9b0c66', 'human-behavior-in-the-social-environment-i', 'Human Behavior in the Social Environment I', 'This syllabus follows a lifespan-development base while incorporating biopsychosocial-spiritual formulation, neuroscience, structural context, trauma/ACEs, culture and power analysis, and applied case assessment. This sequence fits a Social Work core course that prepares students for field education and advanced study. It moves from person-in-environment foundations into development across the life course, then integrates attachment, trauma, culture, power, resilience, and applied assessment.');

