ce to biology alone.", "children": [{"id": "4f69289c-1222-4c66-9f9e-d0e5dbd4019c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brain development and plasticity", "children": [{"id": "d8141278-eb20-4e1c-9be4-6a981d012fe2", "type": "concept", "title": "Neural plasticity"}, {"id": "4ce71e53-9aac-47d8-a4dc-a9f7e5b957b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive function"}, {"id": "c4c4aa36-a16d-490e-bdf9-00dff33e3792", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotion and threat systems"}, {"id": "db2c3565-7dc5-4897-a1f1-50afdc5cdb37", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive periods"}], "description": "Basic neuroscience clarifies how experience can shape brain development and adaptation."}, {"id": "c44cf61c-9a27-4964-af93-44e75a980166", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genes, environment, and temperament", "children": [{"id": "3a506b86-c260-41ff-a917-02cc8e3b3a4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Gene-environment interaction"}, {"id": "98c4273a-d7b3-43e2-a04b-1c3610c20187", "type": "concept", "title": "Epigenetics basics"}, {"id": "cec41a34-d64d-487d-98d3-266e7bcd1be1", "type": "concept", "title": "Temperament"}, {"id": "ca07ce51-51b0-43cb-8705-92dea478347b", "type": "concept", "title": "Differential susceptibility"}], "description": "Students learn to avoid nature-versus-nurture simplifications and understand reciprocal influence."}, {"id": "b811e2a5-a5f9-4f4e-ac37-e1cbbf4a815c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neuroscience in ethical practice", "children": [{"id": "8860c5c0-2622-41e3-84e4-3e41410b0a5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Brain-based explanations"}, {"id": "d3acc304-96f1-4a25-abde-c86ae1c28f9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of neurobiological evidence"}, {"id": "39cd01af-8a77-4ed0-a21a-60cfdd5f1880", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural interpretation of behavior"}, {"id": "a1ab5745-648b-4be4-9d74-8302de9fdc0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Client dignity and agency"}], "description": "Neuroscience can deepen empathy, but it must not become reductionist or stigmatizing."}]}, {"id": "190