s"}, {"id": "bcfa9eec-1fd3-45d0-8844-a5fdd3b1ff8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality in aging"}], "description": "Aging is not one pathway; it varies by health, culture, disability, income, community, and policy."}, {"id": "693a73b1-83e6-404e-8ebc-7bbe689e44f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Loss, grief, and life review", "children": [{"id": "8fdf2527-0534-477e-8f2f-90df029236d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Bereavement"}, {"id": "5d5c5bb3-1d50-40be-9a05-2444ac1bc8d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambiguous loss"}, {"id": "7a1874e7-215d-4b8a-8990-851da8d3a540", "type": "concept", "title": "Life review"}, {"id": "aca26b5f-5e6b-4650-b37f-b8f59ac49480", "type": "concept", "title": "Spirituality and meaning"}], "description": "Later adulthood often brings loss, but also meaning-making, resilience, and relationship depth."}, {"id": "3008c27b-aae2-435f-b6f4-911e21a0c4aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social work with older adults", "children": [{"id": "cc3c7b22-fb29-4901-bcc5-2a6cd234a049", "type": "concept", "title": "Caregiving systems"}, {"id": "57f494e8-8771-4c00-9196-4f07fe625591", "type": "concept", "title": "Elder abuse and neglect"}, {"id": "ac2ba3db-d874-4afa-93b5-be2b8bb5717d", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-term care"}, {"id": "2e866a78-2afc-41b1-bfff-ca5c32d0994f", "type": "concept", "title": "Age-friendly communities"}], "description": "Students connect developmental knowledge to practice, advocacy, and ethical decision-making."}]}, {"id": "e0ada88b-80aa-4cd9-870d-e832c98a3e50", "type": "topic", "title": "Attachment, Relationships, Family Systems, and Relational Development", "description": "Connect attachment and relationship patterns to family life, caregiving, trauma, resilience, and intervention planning.", "children": [{"id": "3fc6835c-ea42-4e42-987e-7bd93d9e3968", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Attachment across the lifespan", "children": [{"id": "f4d4d6c0-3ee9-4b1b-a416-af43f7352402", "type": "concept", "title": "Secure attachment"}, 