 debates"}, {"id": "bcfa9eec-1fd3-45d0-8844-a5fdd3b1ff8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality in aging"}], "description": "Aging is not one pathway; it varies by health, culture, disability, income, community, and policy."}, {"id": "693a73b1-83e6-404e-8ebc-7bbe689e44f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Loss, grief, and life review", "children": [{"id": "8fdf2527-0534-477e-8f2f-90df029236d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Bereavement"}, {"id": "5d5c5bb3-1d50-40be-9a05-2444ac1bc8d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambiguous loss"}, {"id": "7a1874e7-215d-4b8a-8990-851da8d3a540", "type": "concept", "title": "Life review"}, {"id": "aca26b5f-5e6b-4650-b37f-b8f59ac49480", "type": "concept", "title": "Spirituality and meaning"}], "description": "Later adulthood often brings loss, but also meaning-making, resilience, and relationship depth."}, {"id": "3008c27b-aae2-435f-b6f4-911e21a0c4aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social work with older adults", "children": [{"id": "cc3c7b22-fb29-4901-bcc5-2a6cd234a049", "type": "concept", "title": "Caregiving systems"}, {"id": "57f494e8-8771-4c00-9196-4f07fe625591", "type": "concept", "title": "Elder abuse and neglect"}, {"id": "ac2ba3db-d874-4afa-93b5-be2b8bb5717d", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-term care"}, {"id": "2e866a78-2afc-41b1-bfff-ca5c32d0994f", "type": "concept", "title": "Age-friendly communities"}], "description": "Students connect developmental knowledge to practice, advocacy, and ethical decision-making."}]}, {"id": "e0ada88b-80aa-4cd9-870d-e832c98a3e50", "type": "topic", "title": "Attachment, Relationships, Family Systems, and Relational Development", "description": "Connect attachment and relationship patterns to family life, caregiving, trauma, resilience, and intervention planning.", "children": [{"id": "3fc6835c-ea42-4e42-987e-7bd93d9e3968", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Attachment across the lifespan", "children": [{"id": "f4d4d6c0-3ee9-4b1b-a416-af43f7352402", "type": "concept", "title": "Secure attachment"}, {"id": "a2de4fb1-d3dd-4fbb-989d-4ef33ef5ed42", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoidant, ambivalent, and disorganized patterns"}, {"id": "04cbcf2b-a929-418e-aff2-64dfe6fd3687", "type": "concept", "title": "Adult attachment"}, {"id": "8b071922-fcea-4448-9771-d2e6897ea9d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Attachment and trauma"}], "description": "Attachment provides a language for understanding safety, separation, caregiving, and relational expectations."}, {"id": "5b19a4b3-1867-4266-85d2-b3a5b52e975e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family systems and relational context", "children": [{"id": "fa2ac4d4-8340-4e63-87af-2452fba43b66", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundaries and roles"}, {"id": "582df27e-3f26-4216-bdb3-57f2cb5afb26", "type": "concept", "title": "Triangles and patterns"}, {"id": "a582ec82-009a-4905-a70a-b0e480e14900", "type": "concept", "title": "Family life cycle"}, {"id": "d07b7147-1377-43cc-9377-90dedf9fed40", "type": "concept", "title": "Intergenerational transmission"}], "description": "Family systems show how individual behavior can carry relational and intergenerational meaning."}, {"id": "b7211fa7-1521-4ca0-b09c-4fc9390d8d4b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relationship-centered assessment", "children": [{"id": "100f1bf4-9920-48d3-95ed-891f205f651c", "type": "concept", "title": "Support maps"}, {"id": "1a8f4c8d-a4a9-4ae7-ac8f-d2789f1c4715", "type": "concept", "title": "Relationship quality"}, {"id": "28449321-11d9-47ba-84d7-4ec6c2e26227", "type": "concept", "title": "Caregiver capacity"}, {"id": "34cc7a40-a8b2-4182-93bb-d436d9a33ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflict, violence, and safety"}], "description": "Students learn to assess strengths and risks in relationships without blaming individuals for systems-level stress."}]}, {"id": "c134e36e-0409-476f-b001-d575398f8084", "type": "topic", "title": "Stress, Coping, Trauma, ACEs, and Resilience Across the Life Course", "description": "Explain how adversity and trauma affect development while centering resilience, recovery, and protective systems.", "children": [{"id": "56603636-d0e9-4dd5-b95f-28ce1063da9f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stress and coping theory", "children": [{"id": "e2362f64-1af4-43d0-a02a-6ba2a0d99ba9", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary appraisal"}, {"id": "efde58e8-c186-4a03-bbdb-c580e7f28ea2", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem-focused and emotion-focused coping"}, {"id": "c1af7906-1096-482d-8806-f7619c75b13d", "type": "concept", "title": "Social support"}, {"id": "63ad8a83-ff9e-4bdc-a7dd-f5d385cc612b", "type": "concept", "title": "Allostatic load"}], "description": "Stress theory helps students understand demand, appraisal, resources, and adaptation."}, {"id": "3b86f6e9-d625-4fb7-98be-c729bf9ae50e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trauma and ACEs", "children": [{"id": "d6cc8e57-456c-4d14-ae00-6b0cd77f90b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Acute and complex trauma"}, {"id": "1f864cb7-102f-40f6-b855-2c245fb44c00", "type": "concept", "title": "ACEs research"}, {"id": "37b08da9-667d-410a-a2ac-d1ad42f99970", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmental trauma"}, {"id": "cf2c26a6-0b75-4e97-9304-29d2f28d42d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical and community trauma"}], "description": "Trauma and ACEs affect development, health, relationships, and behavior, but they do not define a person."}, {"id": "eaeead88-b8e9-4653-b549-02f2c430f68a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience and protective systems", "children": [{"id": "1a48370f-74b9-42f5-b1bb-8462c289d82d", "type": "concept", "title": "Protective factors"}, {"id": "d836be8f-13b4-42cc-86d2-853c13f0e493", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural resilience"}, {"id": "7d5d533b-0f9a-4376-89d2-0b2f56609eca", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-traumatic growth"}, {"id": "e0adcfa7-c722-4510-912e-ec71ebc021d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed environments"}], "description": "Resilience is built through relationships, resources, meaning, culture, and opportunity."}]}, {"